member.summary:
The BotFather menu description used by the generated ;
missing values produce a compile-time warning (unless  is set)
and values longer than 256 characters are a compile-time error.

Pushes the commands discovered from [Command]-decorated handlers to BotFather via
SetMyCommands. Implemented by the generated PolyBot.PolyBotBotFatherSync;
register it with the generated PolyBotExtensions.AddPolyBotBotFatherSync.

Thread-safe sliding-window rate limiter used by the generated [Throttled] guards;
buckets are keyed by the scope identity (user/chat pair, or bucket 0 for
). Buckets are never evicted — long-running bots with
many distinct users should prefer a scope with fewer keys or a custom limiter.

Persistent storage for finite-state-machine states. Callers pass raw identity keys;
implementations namespace them internally so states of different enum types never
collide for the same raw key.

Moves one step back in the enum's declaration order: any value → previous value;
from the first value (or from no state — a no-op) the stored key is cleared.
Returns the resulting state.
